---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en-CA">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>CITAbleX</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="CITAbleX introduces the CITAble family. CITAble Business is the product that exists today."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header>
        <p class="mark">CITAbleX</p>
        <a href="https://perceptiosphere.com">Perceptiosphere</a>
      </header>
      <main>
        <h1>CITAble Business is the one that exists.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          CITAbleX is the family. CITAble Business is the app: a free framework
          for gathering business context, a workflow upgrade for efforts and
          agentic processes, and a bundle that grounds those workflows in
          Perceptiosphere.
        </p>
        <a class="cta" href="#business">See CITAble Business</a>
        <section class="panel" id="business">
          <h2>CITAble Business</h2>
          <p>
            The free tier helps an organisation structure its context across
            the CITAble bands. Paid workflows track efforts and scheduled
            agentic work from that framework. Perceptiosphere, sold on its own
            or in the bundle, adds the knowledge core inside the same app.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>The family</h2>
          <ul class="family">
            <li class="now">CITAble Business. The product that exists.</li>
            <li>CITAble Futures. The investment umbrella.</li>
            <li>CITAble Horizons. Distressed-firm acquisition and retool.</li>
            <li>CITAble Studios. Startup creation.</li>
            <li>CITAble LTF. The long-term fund.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </main>
      <footer>
        <p>Knowledge lives in Perceptiosphere. Operations live in CITAble Business.</p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
